{
  "name": "scatter_quechua",
  "description": "Quechua (Cuzco-Bolivian Aymara-Quechuan) consonants on the standardized 11-column place axis. Quechua's signature is the 3-way plain/aspirated/ejective stop contrast across velar (k/kh/k') AND uvular (q/qh/q') — visible as a 2-column tall stack in the back-of-mouth area. Palatal ɲ, palatal lateral ʎ. ~22 cells filled.",
